The gender distribution was relatively balanced, with slightly more female than male participants. The mean SBP was calculated from four separate readings and was then used to classify participants into four categories. A mean SBP below 120 mmHg was classified as normal, a mean SBP from 120 to less than 130 mmHg as elevated, a mean SBP from 130 to less than 140 mmHg as Stage 1 hypertension (Stage 1 HT), and a mean SBP of 140 mmHg or higher as Stage 2 hypertension (Stage 2 HT). The majority of participants had a mean SBP between 100 and 120 mmHg, which is also reflected by the normal SBP category being the largest group.

